Carabiners of aluminum: CBP rulings classify climbing carabiners in 7616.99 (other articles of aluminum) or 8308.90 (clasps/hooks for... ), or 7616.99.5190. Some rulings have classified carabiners under 8308.90.30 (other clasps and fasteners...). Actually, known ruling: NY N301... "locking carabiners of aluminum" classified in 7616.99.5190 (other articles of aluminum, other). Others, key-chain carabiners, are 8308.90 or 7616. Heading 8308 covers "clasps, frames with clasps, buckles... for clothing, footwear, bags, travel goods or other made up articles"; climbing carabiners were ruled in 7616.99.51 because not for such articles. A newer ruling for the Belay Master with a plastic clip... the description is "mechanical connectors" and the emphasis on "not motorized" suggests a Chapter 84 or 73 exclusion discussion; the result is likely 7616.99.5190 for aluminum.

The 7616.99.51 subheading covers "Other: Other: Other: Other" — 7616.99.5190 is "Other" (not castings or forgings), with 7616.99.5160 being the cast/forged subheading. I'll go with 7616.99.5190.

{"hts_code": "7616.99.5190", "reason": "Locking climbing carabiners whose predominant material is aluminum are classified as other articles of aluminum under heading 7616, not as clasps of heading 8308."}
